# Generated from: specs/123-register-the-project-verification-gates-and-a-ue-compile-extension-in-steering/requirements.md
Feature: Register the project verification gates in steering

  @SCN001
  Scenario: The manifest registers every project gate
    Given steering/manifest.json
    When it is loaded
    Then repository.format, gate-blender-headless, gate-ue-compile, gate-mcp-schema, gate-shellcheck, and gate-ship-smoke are registered as required validations

  @SCN002
  Scenario: The UE compile extension reports the build result
    Given the project.ue-compile extension
    When gate-ue-compile applies on a macOS host with UE 5.8 and the dogfood project
    Then it runs Build.sh DogfoodEditor Mac Development and reports passed on exit 0 or failed with the error lines

  @SCN003
  Scenario: The tech steering table mirrors the manifest
    Given steering/snippets/project-tech.md
    When a contributor reads the Verification Gates section
    Then every registered validation id appears with its condition, command, and host prerequisite
